***How we will build the AI model***  


Module A — Demand prediction
Train a demand model using price, past sales, calendar features and product information. Begin with LightGBM as a baseline, then implement a small neural network.

Output: predicted units sold for each candidate price.

Module B — Conformal calibration
Hold out a separate calibration period. Use conformalized quantile regression or another suitable conformal method to construct prediction intervals around demand.

Example: predicted demand is 20 units, with an interval of 14–27 units at a nominal 90% coverage level.

Output: lower and upper demand estimates. The stated coverage needs to be tested, especially when demand shifts over time.

Module C — Neural contextual bandit
Give the bandit the current context and a set of candidate prices. It estimates the reward associated with each action and learns from observed or simulated outcomes.

Example candidate prices: ৳90, ৳95, ৳100, ৳105 and ৳110.

Output: a selected price and an updated learning policy.

Module D — Risk-aware price selection
Use the calibrated demand estimates to evaluate downside risk. Add explicit business constraints such as minimum profit margin, inventory limits and maximum permitted price changes.

Output: a price that balances expected profit against risk, rather than simply choosing the highest predicted revenue.
